  <p>
    Government policy is pushing exploration. The ninth round of the Open Acreage Licensing Policy awarded 28 blocks covering about 136,596 sq km, including 12 ultra-deepwater blocks, according to press reports of the award. Deepwater projects take a long time: a typical offshore cycle from licence to production runs 8 to 10 years, according to an S&P Global and EAGE review published in 2025. That is good for long-run subsurface skills, and weak for fast fresher hiring.
  </p>

